bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    seed_lowering_reports_only_first_type_error_2026-11-26, 0, "simple compile/run stop at the first HIR lowering error, so later type errors in the same import closure are never reported. Repro: a file with fn f() -> i64: return 1.5, then fn h() -> text: d.get(\"k\") (Dict<text, text>), then main: compile prints only the E1003 for f, never h. Impact: the 2026-11-26 E1003 sweep (23,072 files) saw 11,832 files exit 1 for other reasons first; an E1003 behind any earlier lowering error stays hidden until that one is fixed, so a 0-hit sweep is a lower bound. Expected: lowering collects type errors per function and reports all of them (or at least every E1003) before failing."

